1
00:01:01,530 --> 00:01:04,530
You ready for the next problem?

2
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:06,530
You know what?

3
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:08,530
I can't look at another number.

4
00:01:08,530 --> 00:01:09,530
How about a lemonade break?

5
00:01:09,530 --> 00:01:10,530
Sure.

6
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:15,530
Oh, by the way,

7
00:01:15,530 --> 00:01:19,530
when is your plane reservation for your flight to Athens?

8
00:01:19,530 --> 00:01:22,530
Sunday. Why?

9
00:01:22,530 --> 00:01:24,530
Would you be able to come over Saturday night?

10
00:01:24,530 --> 00:01:26,530
Yes.

11
00:01:26,530 --> 00:01:28,530
I should be finished packing by then.

12
00:01:28,530 --> 00:01:31,530
My folks are giving me a little graduation party.

13
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:32,530
Terrific!

14
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:35,530
I'll pick you up.

15
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:36,530
That isn't necessary.

16
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:38,530
My dad's letting me borrow the car.

17
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:42,530
Oh, well, that would be very nice.

18
00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:44,530
About eight o'clock?

19
00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:45,530
Eight o'clock is fine.

20
00:01:45,530 --> 00:01:47,530
Great! It's a date.

21
00:01:47,530 --> 00:01:49,530
Who's going to be there?

22
00:01:49,530 --> 00:01:53,530
Just my friend Mike and a few kids from school.

23
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:56,530
I'm going to miss all of you.

24
00:01:56,530 --> 00:01:59,530
You've been like a second family to me.

25
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:01,530
We're going to miss you.

26
00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:04,530
Maybe you could come to visit me in Greece?

27
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:05,530
I'm counting on it.

28
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:06,530
Wonderful!

29
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:09,530
Are you excited about graduating from high school?

30
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:13,530
Sure ... and a little scared.

31
00:02:13,530 --> 00:02:14,530
Scared? Why?

32
00:02:14,530 --> 00:02:16,530
Aren't you a little scared?

33
00:02:16,530 --> 00:02:21,530
I was when I first came to the United States.

34
00:02:21,530 --> 00:02:23,530
I'd never been away from home,

35
00:02:23,530 --> 00:02:26,530
and I didn't know what it would be like.

36
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:31,530
But then I found out that people are the same everywhere

37
00:02:31,530 --> 00:02:33,530
once you get to know them.

38
00:02:33,530 --> 00:02:35,530
I'm glad I got to know you.

39
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:36,530
Thank you.

40
00:02:36,530 --> 00:02:41,530
I'm glad I got to know you--and your family.

41
00:02:41,530 --> 00:02:44,530
Wouldn't it be nice if we could skip the examinations

42
00:02:44,530 --> 00:02:46,530
and get right to the graduation party?

43
00:02:46,530 --> 00:02:48,530
It would be very nice.

44
00:02:48,530 --> 00:02:51,530
But that isn't the way it works.

45
00:02:51,530 --> 00:02:53,530
So ... back to work.

46
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:59,530
Good night, Robbie.

47
00:02:59,530 --> 00:03:00,530
Good night, Mrs. Stewart.

48
00:03:00,530 --> 00:03:01,530
Thank you for dinner.

49
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:02,530
Good night, Alexandra.

50
00:03:02,530 --> 00:03:03,530
Will you be all right?

51
00:03:03,530 --> 00:03:05,530
Yes. The Molinas are waiting for me.

52
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:07,530
Good night, Alexandra.

53
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:10,530
I'll pick you up on Saturday night, OK?

54
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:13,530
Yes.

55
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:16,530
I have to run.

56
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:24,530
Good night, Robbie.

57
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:32,530
She's really a good friend, isn't she?

58
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:34,530
Yeah.

59
00:03:34,530 --> 00:03:37,530
You are going to miss her.

60
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:41,530
Am I going to miss her?

61
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:43,530
That's what I said!

62
00:03:43,530 --> 00:03:46,530
You are going to miss her!

63
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:49,530
I'm going to miss her,

64
00:03:49,530 --> 00:03:53,530
and my math teacher's going to miss her.

65
00:03:53,530 --> 00:03:56,530
Well, you can write to her.

66
00:03:56,530 --> 00:04:10,530
It's not the same.

67
00:04:10,530 --> 00:04:12,530
How does that look, Rob?

68
00:04:12,530 --> 00:04:14,530
Great! Pass me the hammer.

69
00:04:14,530 --> 00:04:15,530
You got it!

70
00:04:15,530 --> 00:04:19,530
You're sure Alexandra's going to be surprised?

71
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:20,530
Absolutely.

72
00:04:20,530 --> 00:04:23,530
She has no idea that the party is in her honor.

73
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:25,530
Millie, did you bring the tapes for dancing? Millie

74
00:04:25,530 --> 00:04:26,530
They're in my bag.

75
00:04:26,530 --> 00:04:27,530
What did you bring?

76
00:04:27,530 --> 00:04:28,530
Some rock 'n' roll.

77
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:30,530
Perfect! Alexandra will love it!

78
00:04:30,530 --> 00:04:34,530
I can't wait to see her face when she walks in here tonight.

79
00:04:34,530 --> 00:04:36,530
What about the cake?

80
00:04:36,530 --> 00:04:38,530
My mom's decorating it right now.

81
00:04:38,530 --> 00:04:44,530
Robbie, there's a phone call for you. Robbie

82
00:04:44,530 --> 00:04:45,530
It's Alexandra.

83
00:04:45,530 --> 00:04:46,530
She sounds upset.

84
00:04:46,530 --> 00:04:47,530
OK.

85
00:04:47,530 --> 00:04:48,530
I'll take it in there.

86
00:04:48,530 --> 00:04:55,530
Hi, Alexandra.

87
00:04:55,530 --> 00:05:01,530
What? You what?

88
00:05:01,530 --> 00:05:04,530
Oh no!
